From ee333298710d8d28826b4baadd7aca40df69713c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaniax17 <bptopteam@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:11:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply section server exclusions to URLTest/Priority (#89, PR
 #90)

Apply section server exclusions to URLTest and Priority groups

Servers excluded by the section-level filter were removed from the section
selector only. URLTest and Priority groups were still built from the full
candidate list, so an excluded server kept carrying traffic through the
group the selector defaults to.

The exclude half of the section filter now trims the candidate pool the
groups are built from. The include half stays selector-only: it can be
group based, and group membership is only known once the groups are built.

---

Format renderFlagEmojis with prettier

The file has been drifting from `yarn format` output since it was added, so
the Frontend CI formatting step fails on any pull request that touches
fe-app-forkop. The workflow only runs on such pull requests, and every run so
far has been queued behind fork approval, so the drift never surfaced.

Reformat the file and rebuild the LuCI bundle from it. No behaviour change.
